<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Gang Gam-chan</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">948–<a href="/years/1031">1031</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/11th-century">11th century</a> · Also known as Kang Kam-chan</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Gang Gam-chan was a Korean scholar-official and general of the Goryeo dynasty. As commander against the third Khitan invasion, he destroyed the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a> army at the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/battle-of-gwiju">Battle of Gwiju</a> in 1019, a victory that secured Goryeo's independence. He is honoured in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a> as one of its great national heroes.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/gang-gam-chan.jpg" alt="Gang Gam-chan" width="320" height="480" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: 공공누리 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:%EA%B0%95%EA%B0%90%EC%B0%AC_%EC%9E%A5%EA%B5%B0_%ED%9D%89%EC%83%81.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
